  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d41a8b62c93e47f198a5b2c4e6f01357, type: 3}
  m_Name: Boat
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: LD60.UI::LD60.UI.StoryComicsData
  background: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f528da51ac12f8d469c3eb563e32a7bc, type: 3}
  blocks:
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f4f592c6c6a85b042b8712c4649dddf8, type: 3}
    subtitle: Money doesn't stink, especially when the whole city smells of smoke
      and gunpowder. The mob's bribes were more than enough for a new life overseas.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af3e0ed028bba1f438921e352262e3b9, type: 3}
    subtitle: '"Smart timing, four-eyes," the scarred gangster chuckled, pocketing
      his cut. "The garrison seals the port in two hours. We''ll be long gone."'
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cf91f8d48b7694646a65564508c4b5dd, type: 3}
    subtitle: The wooden launch smelled of diesel, salt, and freedom. The city was
      already falling behind.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: bde3f4fbd0af9c042979998fc884d667, type: 3}
    subtitle: Fires of revolution lit up the horizon behind the stern. Hell was breaking
      loose back there, but it was someone else's hell now.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fb550f74f962ce640b4afd7b13a90347, type: 3}
    subtitle: The coast guard patrol stayed blind and deaf. Searchlights licked the
      dark waves and died out, letting the launch slip into neutral waters.
  - image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ce01b201a6d08f14894d5f93bdc2c5b4, type: 3}
    subtitle: Let them write their own obituaries. The former editor closed his final
      layout and opened an account at a neutral bank.
